lls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Florida remains a Republican-leaning state in presidential politics, with a partisan lean of roughly five points to the right of the country. The 2028 race is open, with the term-limited president leaving no incumbent on the ballot, and no general-election polls or expert ratings have been published yet. That leaves fundamentals carrying most of the weight, and they point to a modest Republican edge.\n\nRecent headlines add some texture. Democratic results in 2026 special elections and down-ballot contests have generated talk of momentum in Florida, and national coverage describes the state as a potential 2028 proving ground for the party. But the same reporting emphasizes how difficult it has been to reverse the state's rightward shift in recent cycles. The forecast keeps Florida in the Lean Republican column, with wide uncertainty until real polling arrives.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2832, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3401, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.352, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3574, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.3329, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3466, "margin": -4.0}]}